  "text_to_speech": "when i was going through chemotherapy i used to have vivid sound hallucinations [Music] this experience opened the doors to other dimensions of music for me i was able to hear and understand sounds from a totally different angle most of my compositions come from my imagination they come from nostalgia from my experiences and emotions i imagine the melody or the song in my head and i try to sing it to actually make it visible touchable then i try to implement it on the instrument for me music is all about enjoying the experience i would think how can i serve the song so ultimately it can serve the listener to make it more enjoyable as an experience i would write the intro and then i would think what could be the next melody riff or instrument to serve this song this album is a psychedelic rock album i want it to be a cinematic experience for the listener listening to the songs takes you to a trip to a journey at some moments you will listen to the horror and the haunting sound effects and themes but the next moment it will take you to an atmospheric spacey melodies or soundscapes and then it takes you to adrenaline ride of beautiful guitar solos i want the listener not to expect what's going to come next [Music] you",
  "text_to_speech_word_count": 230,
  "timecoded_text_to_speech": [
    {
      "end": "00:00:07.000",
      "start": "00:00:00.000",
      "text": " When I was going through chemotherapy, I used to have vivid sound hallucinations."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:14.000",
      "start": "00:00:07.000",
      "text": " This experience opened the doors to other dimensions of music for me."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:19.000",
      "start": "00:00:14.000",
      "text": " I was able to hear and understand sounds from a totally different angle."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:36.000",
      "start": "00:00:31.000",
      "text": " Most of my compositions come from my imagination."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:40.000",
      "start": "00:00:36.000",
      "text": " They come from nostalgia, from my experiences and emotions."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:47.000",
      "start": "00:00:40.000",
      "text": " I imagine the melody or the song in my head and I try to sing it to actually make it visible, touchable."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:51.000",
      "start": "00:00:47.000",
      "text": " Then I try to implement it on the instrument."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:00:57.000",
      "start": "00:00:54.000",
      "text": " For me music is all about enjoying the experience."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:06.000",
      "start": "00:00:57.000",
      "text": " I would think how can I serve the song so ultimately it can serve the listener to make it more enjoyable as an experience."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:15.000",
      "start": "00:01:06.000",
      "text": " I would write the intro and then I would think what could be the next melody, riff or instrument to serve the song."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:20.000",
      "start": "00:01:17.000",
      "text": " This album is a psychedelic rock album."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:24.000",
      "start": "00:01:20.000",
      "text": " I wanted to be a cinematic experience for the listener."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:28.000",
      "start": "00:01:24.000",
      "text": " Listening to the songs takes you to a trip to a journey."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:34.000",
      "start": "00:01:28.000",
      "text": " At some moments you will listen to the horror and the haunting sound effects and themes."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:41.000",
      "start": "00:01:34.000",
      "text": " But the next moment it will take you to an atmospheric, spacey melodies or sound scapes."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:47.000",
      "start": "00:01:41.000",
      "text": " And then it takes you to adrenaline ride of beautiful guitar solos."
    },
    {
      "end": "00:01:51.000",
      "start": "00:01:47.000",
      "text": " I want the listener not to expect what's going to come next."
